AGPL distribution requirements (must be satisfied before any build that
contains igruntime or liruntime leaves the developer's machine, including testers):
- The combined libgojni.so is a work based on AGPL protocol packages. Distributing it
  requires offering the Corresponding Source of the whole linked runtime
  (this module, go.mod/go.sum, build-android.ps1, and any modifications to
  upstream) under AGPL-3.0-or-later.
- AGPL s13: users interacting with it over a network must be offered source.
  MINI has no server, but the offer must still accompany the app.
- The Android app that loads the runtime is likely a combined work. Options
  recorded in docs/CONNECTOR_ROADMAP.md: (a) license MINI under AGPL,
  (b) obtain a commercial licence or exception from the upstream authors,
  (c) write an independent client. No option has been chosen.
- Until decided: debug builds only, not distributed. Release must not bind
  ./igruntime or ./liruntime.
